          "definition": "I do not have evidence for that in the docs I can access.",
          "term": "abstention"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "cs329z-u02-c11-insufficient-evidence-p04",
          "definition": "If max score < t or the filtered set is empty, abstain.",
          "term": "threshold t"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "cs329z-u02-c11-insufficient-evidence-p03",
          "definition": "Answer with evidence, or I cannot answer from my sources.",
          "term": "third answer"
        }
      ],
      "minutes": 3,
      "recall": [
        {
          "anchor": "cs329z-u02-c11-insufficient-evidence-p04",
          "answer": "A score threshold plus an empty-set rule. Answering wrong costs more than abstaining for factual tasks, so the threshold sits where the expected costs cross.",
          "id": "cs329z-u02-c11-insufficient-evidence-r1",
          "question": "How is the abstention rule set?"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "cs329z-u02-c11-insufficient-evidence-p12",
          "answer": "Break the threshold: corpus drift makes t abstain on half the easy questions. Abstaining on 2+2 needs a fast-path exception.",
          "id": "cs329z-u02-c11-insufficient-evidence-r2",
          "question": "What breaks abstention?"
        }
      ],
      "title": "cs329z-U02-C11: insufficient evidence"
